        {
            "id": "21aa2791-cbae-48b5-b5a2-c441dc9ff7f5",
            "build_id": "00efba95-007c-409f-9a36-6e9c217ea6d0",
            "round_number": 6,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-24T00:57:20.836173+00:00",
            "notes": "[Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) is a nice choice for this round, it offers a useful [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) boost and makes our swings ignore some armor, making tank 1v1s even easier.\n\n[Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) is also a strong choice. It further boosts [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) and [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power), while also negating some enemy bonus [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed).\n\nThis round I would check the enemy tanks build to see what they are building around. If you notice they have a lot of armor, go with [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27). If they have high attack speed, go with [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f). If neither are the case, I would then consider [Plan Z](item_8e9dc830-ad05-413a-bcc9-efc0a23d8625).\n\n [Plan Z](item_8e9dc830-ad05-413a-bcc9-efc0a23d8625) is very strong in a build like this because it boosts attack speed as health gets low. This is strong because of the life steal potential we have with each swing of our hammer. So the lower your health gets, the more life steal you'll get.\n\nAny of those 3 choices are viable, and I'd honestly just recommend choosing which ever you feel you should based on how your game is going or on which works best with your own playstyle.\n\nI don't want to repeat myself too much, by now you should understand what this build is about. Draxx them sklounst.",
